{"name":"Snowfall","hex":"#e0deda","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"snowfall","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An instance of falling of snow.","The amount of snow that falls on one occasion."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/snowfall"}],"entries":[{"title":"Snowfall (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Snowfall is an American crime drama television series, created by John Singleton, Eric Amadio, and Dave Andron for FX. The series premiered on July 5, 2017, and concluded on April 19, 2023, after six seasons consisting of 60 episodes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/78/Snowfalltitlecard.jpg/330px-Snowfalltitlecard.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snowfall_(TV_series)"},{"title":"Snowfall (horse)","blocks":[{"text":"Snowfall was a Japanese-bred Thoroughbred racehorse who won the 2021 Epsom Oaks, Irish Oaks, and Yorkshire Oaks. She showed promising but unremarkable form as a two-year-old in 2020, winning one minor race from seven starts. The following year she improved dramatically, winning the Group 3 Musidora Stakes and then taking the Epsom Oaks by a record margin of sixteen lengths. She went on to win emphatic victories in the Irish Oaks and the Yorkshire Oaks over older horses."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Owner_Mr_Derrick_Smith.svg/330px-Owner_Mr_Derrick_Smith.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snowfall_(horse)"},{"title":"Snow","blocks":[{"text":"Snow is a form of solid atmospheric precipitation consisting of individual ice crystals that grow while suspended in the air—usually within clouds—and then fall, accumulating on the ground, where they undergo further changes. It consists of frozen crystalline water throughout its life cycle, starting when, under suitable conditions, the ice crystals form in the atmosphere, increase to millimeter size, precipitate and accumulate on surfaces, then metamorphose in place, and ultimately melt, slide, or sublimate away."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/CargoNet_Di_12_Euro_4000_L%C3%B8nsdal_-_Bolna.jpg/330px-CargoNet_Di_12_Euro_4000_L%C3%B8nsdal_-_Bolna.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snow"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Feb242007_blizzard.gif/500px-Feb242007_blizzard.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Feb242007_blizzard.gif/1280px-Feb242007_blizzard.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Feb242007_blizzard.gif/500px-Feb242007_blizzard.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Extratropical cyclonic snowstorm, February 24, 2007—(Click for animation.)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFeb242007_blizzard.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Snowsquall_line-Bourrasque_neige_frontal_NOAA.png/500px-Snowsquall_line-Bourrasque_neige_frontal_NOAA.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Snowsquall_line-Bourrasque_neige_frontal_NOAA.png/500px-Snowsquall_line-Bourrasque_neige_frontal_NOAA.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Frontal snowsquall moving toward Boston, Massachusetts","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASnowsquall_line-Bourrasque_neige_frontal_NOAA.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Lake_Effect_Snow_on_Earth.jpg/500px-Lake_Effect_Snow_on_Earth.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_ca